  "evidence": "Oinoe became one of the demes of Athens after 508/7 BCE. In 506 BCE, while the Spartan king Kleomenes invaded Eleusis, the Boeotians captured Oinoe and Hysiai. Athens then beat the Boeotians and took 700 prisoners, ransomed at two minas each.",
  "dated": "",
